title: 'statement-store: size limits for the DHT-affinity and transient statements'

doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    On nodes running the v2 DHT statement path, the store now applies a separate size limit to the
    statements it keeps for DHT affinity and to the transient ones it keeps only until propagated,
    on top of the global limits. Statements kept for explicit affinity alone are bound by the store
    size only. Each limit defaults to the store size and is set with the hidden flags
    `--statement-store-max-dht-affinity-size` and `--statement-store-max-transient-size`. The node
    warns at startup about a limit above half of the store size. A statement its track has no room
    for is rejected with the new reason `TrackFull`, counted as `track_full` in the rejection
    metric; the RPC keeps reporting it as a full store. The statement database migrates to version
    3 on the first start, existing statements count as kept for explicit affinity.

crates:
- name: sp-statement-store
  bump: major
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: minor
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: major
- name: staging-node-cli
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: major
